WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.240
With a show as hilarious as The Office, it's
definitely worth taking the time to watch

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.880
all the blooper reels.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.060
"Ok wait, how do you know it's a warehouse
worker who stunk up the bathroom?"

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.280
"They stink up the bathroom with their smelly
poos and…"

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.280
(Laughs.)

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.580
"They're gonna turn on us, come on."

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:19.419
If you don't have a lot of time on your hands,
never fear: we've rounded up some of the very

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.460
best bloopers from ​The Office​ right
here.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.580
In the season two episode "Office Olympics,"
Michael takes Dwight to the condo he's hoping

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.680
to purchase.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:35.140
Dwight wastes no time making his boss highly
uncomfortable pointing out a string of potential

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:35.640
problems.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.820
"Wow, you'll be paying this off in your mid-seventies…

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.340
Forget about retiring when you're sixty-five."

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:47.960
But in this blooper from the episode, it's
Dwight or rather, actor Rainn Wilson who seems

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.200
really rather uncomfortable… and the reason
why soon becomes clear.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:52.700
"I love you."

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:53.200
"What?"

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.200
"I love you Michael."

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:54.980
"I love you too.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:55.980
What are you even talking about?"

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.600
"I was just talking about…

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:58.980
I farted."

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.880
"Are you kidding me?"

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:05.240
Great to know that actors go through the same
struggles as the rest of us.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.700
Sometimes, actors can really miss the mark.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.820
Take Phyllis Smith, for example.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:14.720
"Phyllis, come on… oh, Jesus… are you
alright?"

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.020
"Phyllis are you okay?"

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:17.640
"I'm okay."

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:22.549
She's not the only Office actor who occasionally
fails at sticking the landing.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:27.540
It seems Brian Baumgartner has yet to master
the subtle art of sitting down.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.420
"Don't you even f------ keep that in there!"

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:42.240
Meanwhile, in the season five episode "Michael
Scott Paper Company," Steve Carell encounters

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.040
some serious car trouble.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:46.040
"F---.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.180
I think I'm gonna need some, um, new pants."

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.500
Hey, no one ever said getting out of cars
was easy.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.660
We all have our things.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:04.460
Well, actor John Krasinski evidently likes
to pretend to get his finger caught in clapperboards.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:05.880
“ow”

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:07.380
“Ow”

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.560
“Ow”

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.560
Who wouldn't want to try their hand at that?

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.600
Clearly Brian Baumgartner was eager to get
in on all the fun.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:19.620
"That's my joke.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:20.700
That's my joke."

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:21.380
"It's funny."

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.620
And here comes Jenna Fischer to show 'em how
it's really done.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:27.180
"Teamwork!

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:28.240
He didn't get me!"

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.840
Everyone, put your hands together for these
clapperboard kooks!

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:39.209
In the season 7 episode "Viewing Party," the
whole staff gathers at Gabe's apartment to

00:02:39.209 --> 00:02:41.650
watch Glee and make homemade pizzas.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:42.140
"So.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.600
These are your cheeses, your hams, your sausages,
your herbs, and your vegetables.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.000
Here's what's been done.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:48.640
Start creating."

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.160
Early on in the episode, Michael is seen throwing
pizza dough in the air… and then this happens:

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.140
"Try to destroy the old ways, Gabe; I will
not let you."

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:03.500
But in one unused take, the scene goes a little
bit differently.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.100
Bon appétit.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.920
"Try to destroy the old ways, Gabe.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:08.660
I will not let you do it."

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:18.120
For an actor, staying in character takes a
lot of hard work.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.440
And it can be tough to remember all those
lines.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:26.599
In a scene from the season 4 episode "Dinner
Party," Dwight unexpectedly arrives at Michael's

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.720
condo with two wine glasses and a creepy date.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.320
"Coming."

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.060
"Hello…"

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:34.860
"What are you doing here?"

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.900
"We came here to eat dinner and to party."

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:42.360
Obviously the scene wasn't shot in one take,
as this ridiculous blooper proves:

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.520
"What are you doing here?"

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:44.620
"Hi, how are you?"

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:45.120
"Hi."

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.080
"I'm not in character yet."

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.120
Hey, at least he's being honest.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:56.499
Throughout season six, Pam does everything
in her power to hold off labor as she wrestles

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.280
with her fear of giving birth.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:04.260
In a scene from the episode "The Delivery:
Part 1," Michael gathers the staff to brainstorm

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:06.439
how to slow down Pam's pregnancy.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:12.160
As Erin reads off a list of ways to stimulate
labor, the group suggests ways of doing the

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.540
exact opposite:

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.920
"Ok, Number Three: Eat spicy foods."

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:17.440
"Okay, yeah — the opposite of that?"

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.040
"Stick spicy food up her butt."

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:19.880
"Nope, nope!"

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:25.000
For obvious reasons, it took a bit of work
before to nail down this particular scene.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:25.760
Take one!

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:27.000
"What is the opposite of that?"

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.280
"Make spicy foods come out of her."

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.500
"No, no…"

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:32.800
Take two!

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.640
"Make spicy foods come out of her."

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.960
"Nope, nope, we're not doing that.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:37.460
Pam?"

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.060
Take three!

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.760
"And the opposite of that?"

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.720
"Make spicy foo … ooohhh."

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.040
Turns out, practice does make perfect.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:53.940
Let's watch the final cut one more time to
bask in the glory.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.400
"Ok, Number Three: Eat spicy foods."

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:57.919
"Okay, yeah — the opposite of that?"

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.620
"Stick spicy food up her butt."

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:00.420
"Nope, nope!"

